<div id="2026-09-03-labour-tracking-plan-and-todos" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-03 — labour tracking added to 3D plan; cross-branch time todos marked AI-authored</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Labour tracking (3d).</strong> Added <b>section 6, "Labour tracking (human time around a print)"</b> to <code>Documentation/3dPrintingPlan.tt</code> (plus a TOC entry). It records the gap: <code>printing_3d_jobs</code> captures machine time and filament, but none of the manual work — cleaning/support removal, picking, kitting, bagging, labelling, packing, QC — so true cost per part is unknown. Includes design rules (AppTime is the only time authority; reuse the log/todo time model rather than adding a table; if a table is unavoidable it is Result-file-first via schema-compare), a 4-phase breakdown with gates, and explicit out-of-scope items (printer telemetry = todo #2334; do not touch the Complete button, which is now correct). Tracked by <b>todo #2390</b> (P1, project #272 DRYER-INT).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>AI attribution.</strong> The 8 cross-branch time/docker todos (#2382&ndash;#2389) were requested by Shanta with bodies drafted by the assistant. Updated each with <code>reporter = ai_assistant</code> and <code>owner = ai_assistant</code>, and appended a footer to every description: "Requested by Shanta; body drafted by the AI assistant (ai_assistant) 2026-09-03. The human owner still owns the decision and the estimate — verify scope before starting." <code>ai_assistant</code> is an established poster in this DB (116 existing todos), so this follows current convention rather than inventing one.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Ranking note (important).</strong> All 9 todos are <code>priority = 1</code> AND <code>is_blocking = 1</code>. Priority 1 alone is not enough: <code>Util::TodoRanking::score_todo</code> dampens P1&rarr;P5 unless <code>_looks_like_real_blocker()</code> matches, which requires <code>is_blocking=1</code> or outage keywords (<code>outage</code>, <code>data loss</code>, <code>merge conflict</code>, <code>[Error]</code>). The create API does not accept <code>is_blocking</code>, so it was set afterwards via <code>/api/todo/update</code>. Anyone creating urgent todos programmatically must do the same or they will be buried.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Coverage.</strong> Todos created: #2382 InventoryAccounting, #2387 + #2388 + #2389 DockerHA (time migration, UTC container timestamps, container identity), #2383 3d, #2384 aisystem, #2385 schema, #2386 helpdesk, #2390 3d labour tracking. Four branches have no todo because their servers were down at the time: git (4004), planning (4005), Documentation (4008) — and DockerHA was initially down but came up on retry.</p>
